•	Number of Nodes Explored
Compare the A* Search result with the route suggested by Google Maps.
1.	Initialize a queue with the start node and its path.
2.	Create an empty visited set.
3.	Set explored nodes count to 0.
4.	While the queue is not empty:
•	Remove the first element from the queue.
•	If the node is not visited:
•	Mark it as visited.
•	Increment explored count.
•	If the node is the goal, return the path, path cost, and explored count.
•	Otherwise, add all neighboring nodes to the queue with their updated paths.
